# Runtime of each bot instance: the default one and any `.<name>` twin
# (a second network = same bot.py, its own env, FIFO, startup and logs).
.env
.env.*
bot.send
bot.send.*
bot.startup
bot.startup.*
bot.log
bot.*.log
aup_watchdog.log
scrub.log

# Who the bot trusts, whose DMs pass, which channels are reserved: per deployment.
# Formats in README; templates are *.example.
bot.trust
bot.trust.*
bot.dmallow*
bot.reserved
reserved_recent.tsv
reserved_recent.tsv.tmp

# E2E (e2e_bridge.py): the key, the Olm state and the pins file are per
# instance and belong outside the repo (README); these catch a misplaced one
# under the README's names, the state's interrupted-save temp file included.
*.key
*.pins
*.e2e.json
.*.e2e.json.*
bot.e2e*
.bot.e2e*

# Deployment config, never in the repo (templates: *.example).
CLAUDE.md
systemd/*.service
systemd/*.timer
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/gate.local.json
.claude/watchd.json

# The skills that run YOUR deployment: copy examples/skills/ here and make them yours.
.claude/skills/start/
.claude/skills/resume/
.claude/skills/close/
.claude/skills/voice/

# The agent's memory, notes, scratch and local helpers.
memory/
tmp/
var/
tools/
scratchpad/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.lock
docs/img/*.png
